te on curl reports 'Nothing to do' and a full dry-run update omits curl while showing unrelated libcurl still eligible for upgrade, confirming curl is specifically excluded while other packages update normally (cmd-dee66d1ca4bd4940). Post-reboot reverification shows the versionlock entry persisted, curl's rpm version is still 8.12.1-4.el10, and a fresh dry-run update again excludes curl (cmd-5415d9effe2b4a43).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-81ed5b80abef4d8c\",\"cmd-dee66d1ca4bd4940\",\"cmd-5415d9effe2b4a43\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1 with recovered state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id 83a0a80f-...-b07a with curl lock in place and systemctl is-system-running=running (cmd-e4ff0ff06b74410c). A native systemctl reboot was issued and acknowledged, with the exec stream closing and subsequent polls timing out/reset, indicating the node went down (cmd-82d24c11a68b4aa5, cmd-ec9b9eac5ebc4091, cmd-45ea4392336f41b3). Connectivity returned with a different boot_id 0f15c938-...-4a3c (cmd-442c1661f88f455a). Post-reboot state confirms recovered service/data state: curl versionlock persisted, curl version unchanged, system health running, and update dry-run still excludes curl (cmd-5415d9effe2b4a43). Cross-checked by the fixed after_executor boot-identity observation matching the same new boot_id and by failed-services/package-health snapshots showing no failures post-reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e4ff0ff06b74410c\",\"cmd-82d24c11a68b4aa5\",\"cmd-ec9b9eac5ebc4091\",\"cmd-45ea4392336f41b3\",\"cmd-442c1661f88f455a\",\"cmd-5415d9effe2b4a43\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"Reviewed the chronological command trace: (1) baseline inspection (read-only), (2) install python3-dnf-plugin-ver